sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as End User
    participant Claude as Claude (MCP client)
    participant MCP as eSIM Hub MCP Server
    participant Stripe
    participant Hub as eSIM Hub APIs (catalog + MM Hub)
    participant SMTP as SMTP (Gmail)

    Note over Claude,MCP: No client auth — the server reads the<br/>mm-hub API key from ESIM_HUB_API_KEY

    User->>Claude: "I need an eSIM for France"
    Claude->>MCP: search_bundles(keyword)
    MCP->>Hub: search catalog (Api-Key from env)
    Hub-->>MCP: matching bundles
    MCP-->>Claude: bundle list (name, price, validity, data)
    Claude-->>User: options — user picks one + gives email

    Claude->>MCP: create_payment_link(bundle_code, user_email)
    MCP->>Hub: get bundle by code (server-side price — never trusted from the model)
    Hub-->>MCP: price + currency + name
    MCP->>Stripe: create Checkout Session<br/>(amount, metadata: bundle_code + user_email)
    Stripe-->>MCP: session id + checkout URL
    MCP-->>Claude: short link /pay/{session_id} + payment_session_id
    Claude-->>User: payment link

    User->>MCP: open GET /pay/{session_id}
    MCP->>Stripe: retrieve session
    MCP-->>User: 302 → Stripe Checkout page
    User->>Stripe: pay (card)
    Stripe-->>User: redirect → /payment/success page
    Stripe--)MCP: webhook checkout.session.completed (signature-verified, logged)

    User->>Claude: "I paid"
    Claude->>MCP: purchase_bundle_and_send_activation(payment_session_id)
    MCP->>Stripe: retrieve session + PaymentIntent

    alt session not found or payment_status != paid
        MCP-->>Claude: error — payment not completed, ask user to pay first
    else already fulfilled (PaymentIntent has esim_order_id)
        MCP-->>Claude: error — payment already used for order X
    else paid and unfulfilled
        Note over MCP: bundle_code + user_email are read from the<br/>paid session's metadata — order always matches payment
        MCP->>Hub: create reseller order (bundle, email)
        Hub-->>MCP: orderId + SMDP+ address
        MCP->>Stripe: stamp esim_order_id on PaymentIntent<br/>(one payment = one order, survives restarts)
        MCP->>Hub: get activation code (orderId)
        Hub-->>MCP: activation code
        Note over MCP: build LPA URL<br/>LPA:1$smdp$code + QR image
        MCP->>SMTP: send activation email (QR attached)
        SMTP-->>User: activation email in inbox
        MCP-->>Claude: success (orderId, activation_url, email_sent)
        Claude-->>User: "Your eSIM is ready — check your email"
    end
